Fixed and committed as d9f590c3. An unknown top-level flag now stops yoyo with exit 2 before anything is sent:

```
$ yoyo --modle claude-haiku-4-5 -p hi
error: unknown flag '--modle' (did you mean --model?). Nothing was sent to the model. Run yoyo --help for the list of flags.
$ echo $?
2
```

yoyo log --bogus is refused the same way. Before, it sent "log" as a prompt and exited 0.

Census of my own scripts (done before the code change): I listed every yoyo call in scripts/*.sh, scripts/bench/, .github/workflows/ and .github/actions/, including line continuations, the YOYO_SKILL_FLAGS array and the fallback/extra-flags variables. The flags they pass are --model, --skills, --fallback, --context-strategy, --max-turns, --prompt, -p and --output-format, and all of them are in KNOWN_FLAGS. The workflows run plain yoyo < "$PROMPT". Subcommand calls such as risk snapshot and gasp … are handled before this check runs. So the refusal can't stop my own loop.

What gets refused: a word before -- that starts with -, isn't - or --, has no spaces, isn't the value of a flag that takes one, and isn't a known flag. --model=x is refused with a hint to write the value as its own word. These behave exactly as before and still only warn:
• anything after --
• a quoted prompt that starts with -, like "- fix the list"
• a subcommand's own flags, like yoyo diff --stat

Changes:
• src/cli_config.rs: unknown_flag_refusal sits next to bad_numeric_flag_refusal. It suggests the nearest flag within edit distance 2 by reusing commands::closest_match. It escapes control bytes and uses no special glyphs. Table tests and a control-byte test are included.
• src/cli.rs: 4 new lines at the call site, placed before the trust prompt, the setup wizard and any request. I updated the file's size entry in tests/module_size.rs to 7877.
• tests/unknown_flag_refusal.rs: runs the real binary against a local stub that counts requests, with provider keys removed from the environment. The refused runs reach the stub 0 times. The cases that must still work do: known flags, a correctly spelled --model reaching the stub, -- keeping the old warning, and yoyo diff --stat in a temporary git repo.
• Changed existing tests: four tests in tests/integration.rs and one in src/cli.rs asserted the old warning, and they now expect the refusal (error:, exit 2). The one in cli.rs used to check that a typo like --safe leaves safe mode off; it now checks the typo is refused.
• CHANGELOG.md and docs/src/usage/commands.md describe the new behaviour.

Checks: I disabled the new call site, and exactly the two refusal tests failed. With it restored, everything passes: clippy, fmt, cargo test (7113 passed, 0 failed) and tests/harness_logic.sh (321 passed).

Not fixed in this change (posted on #1109, since the push will close it): yoyo -- hi still warns "Unknown flag '--'", and words that look like flags after -- are still dropped from the prompt instead of being sent as text.
